mui-stage-rt is MIT licensed, as is the rest of MUI. It ports no GPL code
(nothing from Blender or Cycles). It follows these permissively licensed
sources and published papers:

- pbrt-v4, Matt Pharr, Wenzel Jakob and Greg Humphreys, Apache License 2.0
  (https://github.com/mmp/pbrt-v4): the dielectric Fresnel equations and
  refraction conventions in rt.wgsl (`fresnel`, the refract/TIR handling).
- Bruce Walter, Stephen R. Marschner, Hongsong Li and Kenneth E. Torrance,
  "Microfacet Models for Refraction through Rough Surfaces", EGSR 2007: GGX
  sampling and the rough-transmission weight (`ggx_sample`, `ggx_g1`,
  `ggx_d`, eq. 41).
- Holger Dammertz, Daniel Sewtz, Johannes Hanika and Hendrik P. A. Lensch,
  "Edge-Avoiding A-Trous Wavelet Transform for fast Global Illumination
  Filtering", HPG 2010, and Christoph Schied et al., "Spatiotemporal
  Variance-Guided Filtering", HPG 2017: the edge-stopping a-trous filter
  (`denoise`).
- Mark Jarzynski and Marc Olano, "Hash Functions for GPU Rendering", JCGT
  2020: the PCG hash (`pcg`).
- Martin Roberts, "The Unreasonable Effectiveness of Quasirandom Sequences"
  (2018): the R2 pixel sequence.
- The sky is mui-stage's own (MIT), spliced in from stage.wgsl.
